e:readme (start) 0.91/0.11 pass.',\n\n  Line 127:     expectedHead: 'Advisor: live; use sk-review 0.61/0.28 pass.',\n\n  Line 139:     expectedHead: 'Advisor: live; use sk-code → /doctor:review gate 0.77/0.20 pass.',\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/references/hook-contract.md:\n  Line 185:     \"additionalContext\": \"Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:\n  Line 238: | The brief says `Advisor: stale`, or `advisor_recommend` returns `degraded: true` | The daemon was unreachable, so the CLI answered from the Python local scorer. | A degraded answer is usable. Check `python3` is on PATH and retry; pass `--warm-only` to make the CLI fail instead of degrading. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/tests/test_measure_rule_compliance.py:\n  Line 64:             \"attachment\": {\"type\": \"hook_additional_context\", \"content\": [text], \"hookName\": \"SessionStart\"}}\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/ux-hooks/cli-hook-transport-down-fail-open.md:\n  Line 14: This scenario verifies the transport-down behavior of the surviving runtime hook integrations. The Claude skill-advisor `user-prompt-submit` hook, which the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters also spawn, runs the CLI through the fallback helper with `--no-warm-only`, so the CLI owns daemon reachability. The memory-backed session-prime, compact-inject, session-stop and session-start hooks were removed with their server, so the advisor hook is the remaining consumer of this contract. A casual prompt such as `hello` never reaches the CLI: the prompt gate declines it first and the hook prints `Advisor: prompt skipped.` On a cold socket the CLI starts the launcher and waits at most 5 s, then answers from the local scorer. The hook marks the answer degraded and renders it as stale (`Advisor: stale`). When the hook budget ends first, the hook exits 0 and prints `Advisor: outage (fail_open); route by hand:` above the directives. In every case the hook exits 0 and never blocks the prompt.\n\n  Line 26: - Expected signals: All three runs exit 0. The `short:` first line starts with `Advisor: outage (fail_open); route by hand:`. The `casual:` first line is `Advisor: prompt skipped.` The `default:` first line starts with `Advisor: live;`, `Advisor: stale;` or `Advisor: outage (fail_open);`.\n\n  Line 87: - The `default:` first line starts with `Advisor: live;`, `Advisor: stale;` or `Advisor: outage (fail_open);`. Which one appears depends on whether the CLI starts a daemon for the sandbox socket in time and whether the local scorer answers first. All three are a pass.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs:\n  Line 736:   const advisorTail = '\\n\\nAdvisor: live; use sk-code 0.9/0.2 pass.\\nDirectives:\\n- Comment hygiene [HARD BLOCK]: NEVER embed ADR- ids in code comments\\n- Governor: move on; write the durable WHY';\n\n  Line 743:     'review the auth module\\n\\nAdvisor: live; use sk-code 0.9/0.2 pass.',\n\n  Line 759:     ' review the auth module\\n\\nAdvisor: live; use sk-code 0.9/0.2 pass.',\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/copilot-user-prompt-submit-hook.vitest.ts:\n  Line 53:   return top ? `Advisor: live; use ${top.skill} ${top.confidence}/${top.uncertainty} pass.` : null;\n\n  Line 139:     expect(written).toContain('Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.');\n\n  Line 250:     expect(result?.brief).toBe('Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.');\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/directive-lifecycle-adapter-parity.vitest.ts:\n  Line 13: const FULL = 'Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.\\nDirectives:\\n- Comment hygiene';\n\n  Line 14: const ROUTE_ONLY = 'Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.';\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/cli/daemon-cli-reference.md:\n  Line 50: When the daemon cannot be reached, a prompt-time hook still answers from the degraded local path and the brief reads `Advisor: stale` rather than `Advisor: live`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/cli-runtime-warm-only-fallbacks.md:\n  Line 28: `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` (system-skill-advisor hooks) runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only --timeout-ms` (warm calls measured 117-198 ms) because the CLI is the only component that starts the daemon. On a cold socket the CLI starts the launcher and waits for the daemon within a bounded cold-start window of at most 5 seconds. If the daemon does not answer in that window `advisor_recommend` answers from the local Python scorer, marked degraded, and the hook shows `Advisor: stale`.\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":86,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 86 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle-vectors.json:\n  Line 3:   \"brief\": \"Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.\\nDirectives:\\n- Comment hygiene\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:\n  Line 44: The single front door is the daemon-backed CLI at `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`, which speaks the advisor's own newline-delimited protocol over a unix socket. When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI answers from the Python scorer at `runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` and marks the response degraded, so the prompt-time brief reports `Advisor: stale` rather than claiming live. The skill also owns the documentation for the OpenCode plugin surface and the `/goal` plugin.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:\n  Line 333:   - If the daemon stays unreachable, the CLI answers from the local Python scorer and marks the result degraded. The brief then renders `Advisor: stale` instead of claiming live.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/manual-testing-playbook/doctor-commands/doctor-routing-helper-handoff.md:\n  Line 34:   - The first brief starts `Advisor: live; use /doctor:helper`.\n\n  Line 35:   - The second brief starts `Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop`, and its second line is exactly `Also: /doctor:helper`.\n\n  Line 36:   - The third brief starts `Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop`, and `/doctor:` appears nowhere in it.\n\n  Line 71: - `pb-doc-406a` starts `Advisor: live; use /doctor:helper`, because no skill matches and the helper's ranker reads the prompt as an `/doctor:agents-md` problem.\n\n  Line 72: - `pb-doc-406b` starts `Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop` and its second line is exactly `Also: /doctor:helper`. \"Never converges\" names a wrong state, so the hand-off shows beside the passing skill.\n\n  Line 73: - `pb-doc-406c` starts `Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop` and prints no `/doctor:` text. \"Drift\" is a bare problem word, which does not count beside a passing skill.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:\n  Line 82: | SAD-003 | Claude hook additional context | Confirm prompt-time hook surfaces advisor context and fails open safely | `Role: Runtime hook operator. Context: current MCP server build and Claude UserPromptSubmit hook script. Action: pipe a realistic prompt payload into the hook, capture stdout and stderr separately and inspect additional context plus diagnostics. Format: return PASS or FAIL with context presence, prompt-safety result and exit code.` | 1. `bash: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build` -> 2. `bash: mkdir -p /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook` -> 3. `bash:` resolve `DIAG` with `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(process.cwd())` and record its line count, as in step 2 above -> 4. `bash: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"help me commit my changes\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\"}' \\| SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.stdout.json 2> /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.shim-stderr.txt` -> 5. `bash: echo \"Exit: $?\"` -> 6. `bash: tail -n 1 \"$DIAG\"` -> 7. `bash:` pipe the same payload into `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` and capture its stderr | Exit code 0. Stdout is valid JSON and contains `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. For a matching prompt it starts with `Advisor:` and a freshness word (`live` or `stale`). With no brief it starts with one of the three status lines: `Advisor: outage (`, `Advisor: no skill matched.` or `Advisor: prompt skipped.` `{}` means the shim failed, which is a FAIL. The shim's own stderr is empty. The diagnostics JSONL gains one line, and that record has `runtime: \"claude\"`, `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The inner hook's stderr carries the same record shape. The raw prompt literal is absent from both | Preconditions:<br>`SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=UNSET`<br>`hook script exists`<br><br>Shim transcript, 2026-09-26, stdout ab...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/opencode-plugin-bridge.md:\n  Line 77: - Native success carries an `Advisor:` brief rendered from the CLI payload. The brief starts with `Advisor: live;` when the daemon answered with a live graph, and with `Advisor: stale;` when the daemon answered with a stale graph or the CLI answered from its local scorer. The plugin's internal route label is not shown by any step and is not a pass criterion.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/directive-dedup.test.ts:\n  Line 22: const HEAD = 'Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.';\n\n  Line 31: const HEAD_CHANGED = 'Advisor: live; use sk-doc 0.95/0.12 pass.';\n\n  Line 175:     // FULL begins with \"Advisor: live; …\" — the head case, advisor working.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.test.ts:\n  Line 165:     ['injected capsule is not an override', 'devin -p \"task\"', 'run the task\\n\\nAdvisor: live; use cli-devin 0.95/0.20 pass.', true],\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/manual-testing-playbook/plugin-utilization/system-skill-advisor.md:\n  Line 31: - Expected signals: the system prompt holds `Advisor: live;` naming `sk-git`. The recorded line is `Advisor: live; ambiguous: sk-git 0.84/0.16 vs system-skill-advisor 0.82/0.16 pass.` With the kill switch the `Advisor:` line count drops to 0.\n\n  Line 34: - Pass/fail: PASS if the live run carries the `Advisor: live;` line naming `sk-git` and the switch run carries 0 lines. FAIL if the line is absent, names no skill, or survives the switch.\n\n  Line 45: 3. v1 check: read the captured system prompt and confirm the `Advisor: live;` line names `sk-git`. Then rerun with `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` as